1
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,940
(This story is entirely fictional)

2
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:30,880
(All these years,)

3
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,520
(Based on Doctor Qin: Executer)
(I've always felt like Wen never left.)

4
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:36,040
(I never threw away any of her things.)

5
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:38,080
(I polish)

6
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,880
(every pair of her shoes once a month.)

7
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,920
(But I never noticed...)

8
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:45,240
(Perhaps the heavens took pity on me)

9
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:47,720
(and let me find the USB drive.)

10
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,880
(I don't know whose filthy voices)

11
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:02,400
(those were.)

12
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,800
(Recent search: "Jin Keke")
(But I knew for sure)

13
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:09,080
(that whatever happened to Xia Wen
had to do with Jin Keke.)

14
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:14,920
Wang Xiaowu,

15
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:18,040
do you have Jin Keke's contact info?

16
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,680
Yeah, the one who dropped out.

17
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:23,240
Shangshi District?

18
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:25,640
Baiyun Street?

19
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:28,920
Phone. Do you have her phone number?

20
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:08,380
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 24=

21
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,680
Offi... officer, what's going on?

22
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:20,920
Where's Song Yalan?

23
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,720
Where's Song Yalan,
the one who lives here?

24
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:23,720
Song Yalan?

25
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:26,000
She left this morning with a suitcase.

26
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,360
Said she was going on vacation.

27
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,680
Asked me to watch the place for her.

28
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:31,800
(Su Shi)

29
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:37,420
(Le Tianyi/The Kneeling Man.
Cowardice, Submission, Punching-down)

30
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:38,800
(He treats people like animals.)

31
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:48,340
(Good Luck Hot Pot)

32
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:49,980
(Zhang Xiaodong-Sanhao Finance-Victims;
Jin Keke, Jin Qingshan)

33
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:52,220
(Liu Sanhao: dirtier hands, lower rank;
Jin Keke, Jin Qingshan)

34
00:02:58,200 --> 00:02:59,000
Mr. Qin.

35
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,200
Song Yalan fled.

36
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:02,720
They've issued a wanted notice.

37
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:06,640
Ms. Song

38
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:09,080
is not that simple.

39
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,120
(Jin Keke dropped out.)

40
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:18,840
(She vanished for years.)

41
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:20,800
(I asked around for a long time,)

42
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:23,040
(Blissful Lane Restaurant)
(and finally found her.)

43
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,200
What are you dawdling for?

44
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:25,560
You act like you own the place.

45
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:30,880
You move like a snail!
Just looking at you pisses me off!

46
00:03:42,580 --> 00:03:44,740
(Dialing 12320 Health Hotline)

47
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:47,880
I want to report

48
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,080
Blissful Lane Restaurant

49
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:51,440
for hiring people
without health certificates.

50
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:53,040
And using fake IDs.

51
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:57,680
We all have them.

52
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:59,760
Most of us have health certificates.

53
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,400
There's just one new girl.

54
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,800
Her certificate
is still being processed.

55
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,600
Save it. That doesn't fly here.

56
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:05,360
We go by the facts.

57
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,560
You either have it or you don't.

58
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:07,880
You gotta come back tomorrow.

59
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:08,600
Rules are rules.

60
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:09,800
We handle things by the book.

61
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,160
Listen... listen to me.

62
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:14,880
Was it you who reported us?

63
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:18,440
Because your health certificate
didn't come through,

64
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:19,760
we're getting fined now!

65
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:21,000
You're

66
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,920
not just filthy on the outside.
You're rotten to the core!

67
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:24,280
Get out of here!

68
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:25,960
You're not getting a single cent today!

69
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:26,720
Get lost!

70
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:48,800
Why do you always pick on me? Why?

71
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:54,800
(Jin Keke)

72
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:57,080
(was like a frightened rat,)

73
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:59,320
(hiding in the filthiest corner.)

74
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:03,560
(She was alive,
but worse off than dead.)

75
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:07,600
(Poverty, debt, discrimination,
and relentless hunting.)

76
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,400
(That's exactly what I needed.)

77
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,880
(I'll follow her wherever she goes.)

78
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,080
(I'll make her go through
everything Wen went through.)

79
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,960
(Fear, despair,
and having nowhere left to turn.)

80
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,600
Jin Keke moved out?

81
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:33,480
A while ago.

82
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:35,400
Barely three months
after Mr. Jin's accident,

83
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:37,040
I took this place over.

84
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,200
Don't you think that's bad luck?

85
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,520
Mr. Jin was a good man.

86
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:44,920
I don't mind.

87
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:47,640
You got a death wish?

88
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,600
Let me tell you,

89
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:51,560
every last one of those Jins
owes me money!

90
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:00,160
Call me San.

91
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,840
Sa... San.

92
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:06,120
You pretty little thing.

93
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:18,580
(Cotton Mill Family Housing,
Building 3, Room 402)

94
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:27,640
(I told Liu Sanhao Jin Keke's address.)

95
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:28,760
(I hate her.)

96
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:31,000
(I hate that she wouldn't tell me)

97
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,640
(what happened that night.)

98
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:34,880
(I just don't want her to have it easy.)

99
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:37,760
(That way I'd have a chance
to get close to her,)

100
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:42,080
(and turn her into my tool for revenge.)

101
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:44,160
You think your father's dead,

102
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:46,040
so the debt's paid off?

103
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:48,760
You guys drove my dad to his death!

104
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:50,360
What more do you want?

105
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,360
I'm telling you!

106
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:53,320
If you don't pay up next month,

107
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,880
I'll sell you to the mountains!

108
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:56,720
I don't have the money to pay you back!

109
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:00,720
No money?

110
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,600
Then you can pay another way.

111
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,400
Shengchan, come here.

112
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,440
I'm not into kids.

113
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,080
Don't move.

114
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:12,920
Stop shining that!

115
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,520
Who are you?

116
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,760
I already called the cops!

117
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:23,500
(Dialing Emergency Number)

118
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:24,960
Sanhao.

119
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,240
110.

120
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,160
Let's go now.

121
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:27,840
What a buzzkill!

122
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:28,600
Let's go!

123
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:30,480
Old hag, you...

124
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:32,280
Just you wait.

125
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:10,640
(Pain is the best catalyst.)

126
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:13,200
(Only when a person's body and dignity)

127
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:14,600
(are completely crushed)

128
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:18,000
(does a crack appear in her soul,)

129
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:20,440
(one I can slip into.)

130
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:25,380
(I'm sorry, Mom. Mom, I miss you.)

131
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:45,620
(Mom, I miss you. I miss you.)

132
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:58,580
Don't move. You've got a fever.

133
00:09:03,380 --> 00:09:04,340
Ms. Song.

134
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:07,980
You followed me?

135
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:10,220
You're injured. Lie down.

136
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:12,780
Why did you save me?

137
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:16,420
Because you're my student,

138
00:09:18,980 --> 00:09:20,740
and my daughter's best friend.

139
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:26,900
Why can't you just leave me alone?

140
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:29,820
I really don't know anything!

141
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:36,140
Look at you.

142
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:39,900
You're so feverish
you're talking nonsense.

143
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:43,380
Good girl, lie down.

144
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:46,340
Come on.

145
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:02,060
A good sleep and you'll be fine.

146
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:16,940
No!

147
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:53,340
You're up.

148
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:56,460
Wash your face. Let's eat.

149
00:11:15,140 --> 00:11:18,210
(Outstanding Teacher, Song Yalan)

150
00:11:21,460 --> 00:11:25,300
(In Loving Memory
of My Daughter, Xia Wen)

151
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:40,700
Here, take your medicine.

152
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:44,180
Ms. Song,

153
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:45,500
thank you.

154
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:49,300
I'm fine now. I should go.

155
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:50,780
Go?

156
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:53,460
Where could you go?

157
00:11:54,260 --> 00:11:56,780
Those people out there
are all looking for you.

158
00:11:58,420 --> 00:11:59,500
That's my problem.

159
00:12:00,860 --> 00:12:02,540
You've already helped me enough.

160
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:10,540
Okay.

161
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:13,300
Then take care of yourself.

162
00:12:25,060 --> 00:12:27,300
What... what are you doing?

163
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:29,100
Stay here for now.

164
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:31,460
It's safer here.

165
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:34,900
You can leave once those people stop

166
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:37,340
looking for you.

167
00:12:50,460 --> 00:12:53,900
Keke, stay alive.

168
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:58,260
Even if it's just for Wen's sake.

169
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:00,340
Just keep living.

170
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:22,340
(In Loving Memory
of My Daughter, Xia Wen)

171
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:42,700
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

172
00:13:43,290 --> 00:13:47,590
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

173
